From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Shenk <kevin@avu.nu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:18:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Translate without user-defined functions where the
 connection has none

Six call sites hand over to the overlay's WP_SQLite_UDF_Free_Translator:
the MySQL functions normally emulated with UDFs become plain SQLite
expressions (or are evaluated in PHP for constant arguments), IF() becomes
CASE, LIKE BINARY patterns are converted at translation time, strict-mode
errors are raised through a malformed-JSON trick instead of THROW(),
REGEXP goes to the backend's native operator where the connection has one
(and is refused with a clear cause where it has none), and seeded RAND()
is refused with a clear cause.
---
 .../src/sqlite/class-wp-mysql-on-sqlite.php   | 95 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 86 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/mysql-on-sqlite/src/sqlite/class-wp-mysql-on-sqlite.php b/packages/mysql-on-sqlite/src/sqlite/class-wp-mysql-on-sqlite.php
